@start **The window opens on the anchor.** Column 0, `fruA`, is a spine column carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 99.6% of them, at 0.08 bits {S1}.

@variable **A short variable stretch follows**, columns 1 to 2, `psuK` to `psuG`, carried by 89 to 90%, [[pseudouridine metabolism]] {S2, Q}. Then a spine, columns 7 to 11, `yeiI` to `lysP`, carried by 92 to 94%, fewest named at column 7, 61% {S7}. Through columns 28 to 30 a branch of 3 shell families runs in 10%, and through columns 70 to 76 a branch of 7 shell families runs in 10 to 11% {S10.b28, S12.b70}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 96 against 87%, and hesitates less there, 0.19 against 0.54 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 28, `yohP`, is a fork column, at 0.85 bits {H, M}.

@end **The window ends in fork and variable columns.** Columns 42 to 79 are carried by 41 to 88%, in a region of plasticity in 5 to 78% of calls {S12}. The last column is `yegQ`, in 41% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 91% of genes**, 0.39 bits on average, perplexity 1.5 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.95 against 0.22 bits, and names fewer genes, 75% against 96% {C}.

